<title>DENMARK: FORECAST-Danish May jobless seen unchanged 7.9 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Danish May jobless seen unchanged 7.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish May unemployment is seen unchanged from April at 7.9 percent, according to a Reuter survey of nine economists.</p>
<p>But they said that although there was no change as a percentage of the workforce, the seasonally-adjusted number of jobless actually showed a fall to 219,000 from 221,300 in April.</p>
<p>Most new jobs, they said, were in processing industries, they said.</p>
<p>The May employment data is to be published by the national statistics office at 0730 GMT on Thursday.</p>
<p>--Stig Pedersen, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650</p>
